==English==

===Etymology===
From ''read the Riot Act''. See sense 2. 

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb|head=[[read]] [[(]][[someone]][[)]] [[the]] [[riot]] [[act]]}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[scold]] or [[berate]] somebody; to [[reprimand]].
#: ''She really '''read him the riot act''' about his smoking habit.''
# {{lb|en|British|Commonwealth||archaic|historic}} To [[give]] a formal [[warning]] for a [[riot|riotous assembly]] to [[disperse]], usually through reading a section of the {{w|Riot Act}}.
====Synonyms====
* See also [[Wikisaurus:reprehend]]

